maria: Heads-up — I'm starting a migration of the troubleshooting doc that covers 429s, timeouts, context limits, and fallback behavior into the unified SDK v2 examples. Need owners for: retry snippets, streaming fallback, context-trim example, and QA checklist.

alex: I can own retry/backoff examples. Should we change semantics from v1?

maria: Two main changes to call out: v2 exposes a builtin retry policy object (retry: {maxAttempts, jitter, backoffMs}) and a context-trim helper that we want to surface. Also show explicit fallback to smaller model on 429s.

alex: Cool. Drafted a snippet — please sanity-check.

alex: ```js
// v2 SDK: retry + fallback example
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
async function generateWithFallback(prompt) {
  try {
    return await client.responses.create({
      model: "open-large-v1",
      input: prompt,
      retry: { maxAttempts: 3, jitter: true, backoffMs: 250 }
    });
  } catch (e) {
    if (e.code === 429) {
      // immediate fallback to cheaper / lower-latency variant
      return await client.responses.create({ model: "open-small-v1", input: prompt });
    }
    throw e;
  }
}
```

maria: Nice. Add a short note about idempotency for streaming requests (cancel vs retry).

tyler: I can run perf/latency checks for the fallback pattern. Will measure 95p latency for both primary and fallback models and paste numbers in the doc. @linda can you cover QA test cases?

linda: Yes — creating a checklist. Items: reproduce 429 (rate limit), simulated timeout, context-trim correctness (long prompt -> trimmed), streaming interrupt handling, and link verification. Need a small harness to produce 429 reliably for QA.

maria: For the harness, use this curl to hit the staging quota limiter: (small snippet)

maria: ```bash
# hammer staging to produce 429s (use with care)
for i in {1..40}; do
  curl -s -X POST https://staging.redwood.dev/v2/responses -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" -d '{"model":"open-large-v1","input":"hi"}' &
done
wait
```

linda: Perfect — I'll add that as a QA reproduction step and capture the response body we expect for 429s (error.code and retry_after).

maria: Also we need to fix two broken anchors I found while porting: /docs/error-handling#rate-limits -> now #too-many-requests and /docs/streaming#interrupt -> changed to #streaming-fallback. Marking link fixes in the PR.

alex: I'll include a short migration note at top: "If you relied on client-side retries in v1, use retry: {} in v2 and account for streaming idempotency." Keep it terse.

maria: QA note: please include expected log snippets so SRE can correlate. Example: `ERROR resp: code=429 route=/v2/responses client=team-a retry_after=1.2s`

linda: Will add sample log lines and a tiny checks list: pass/fail for each case plus screenshots where applicable.

docs-bot: linkcheck queued for PR #3587; label added: docs/linkcheck.

maria: Great. Plan: alex will open a single PR that updates troubleshooting doc and samples; linda will attach QA checklist and reproduction harness; tyler will add perf numbers; I'll do a quick copy-edit and merge to canary once linkcheck passes.

tyler: ETA for perf numbers: EOD tomorrow.

alex: I'll open the draft PR today and add `[WIP]` tag. Will ping when ready for review.

maria: Thanks team :thumbsup: Also note: update the SDK snippet index page to point to new example path `/docs/sdk/v2/error-handling/retries-and-fallbacks`.

deploy-bot: Reminder — when ready run `/deploy-docs canary` to push to the canary site.

maria: Ok locking owners: alex (snippets + PR), linda (QA + harness), tyler (perf), maria (merge + copyedit). I'll post back with PR link. :eyes:
